      <h2>San Antonio Tiny Home Builders Who Design for Your Lot First</h2>
      <p>San Antonio has quietly become one of the best cities in Texas for small-home living. Older neighborhoods inside Loop 410 have deep lots with alley access, newer subdivisions in the north and west have room behind the house for a guest suite, and the ranch land just past Loop 1604 is a natural fit for a park model or tiny house on wheels. As tiny home builders in San Antonio, Cowboy Tiny Homes starts every project by looking at the land, not a catalog.</p>
      <p>That means we ask the questions that decide what you can actually build: Is the lot inside city limits or in unincorporated Bexar County? Is there an HOA? Where do water, sewer and electric come in? Is there an alley, a slope or a drainage easement? The answers point you toward the right home type before you spend money on drawings.</p>

      <h2>What We Build in San Antonio</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
